From: LinBox <linbox@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] LinBox box64 bionic: bridge bionic-only libc/liblog symbols for the x86_64-bionic closure

Fixes the remaining "Error: Symbol ... not found, cannot apply
R_X86_64_JUMP_SLOT" landmines from the 2026-11-14 device logs
(containers 000 wineboot / 1080 taskmgr, box64 v0.4.4 bionic form):

  [BOX64] Error: Symbol __android_log_print not found ... in
      .../wine/lib/x86_64-bionic/libandroid-shmem.so (ver=1 / (none))
  [BOX64] Error: Symbol __gnu_strerror_r not found ... in
      .../wine/lib/x86_64-bionic/libfontconfig.so (optver=2 / LIBC)
  [BOX64] Error: Symbol __FD_SET_chk / __FD_ISSET_chk not found ... in
      .../wine/lib/x86_64-bionic/libX11.so (optver=2 / LIBC)

and the 2026-11-14 follow-up batch (containers 92 wine-9.2-x86_64 /
10889 hangover-11.16 wineboot, both wine flavors, both closures):

  [BOX64] Error: Symbol __fseterr not found ... in
      .../wine-9.2-x86_64/lib/x86_64-bionic/libunistring.so (optver=4 / LIBC_P)
  [BOX64] Error: Symbol __system_property_get not found ... in
      .../wine/lib/x86_64-bionic/libglib-2.0.so (optver=2 / LIBC)
  [BOX64] Error: Symbol __system_property_find not found ... in
      .../wine/lib/x86_64-bionic/libicuuc.so.78 (optver=2 / LIBC)
  [BOX64] Error: Symbol __strchr_chk / __strlen_chk not found ... in
      .../wine/lib/x86_64-bionic/libx265.so (optver=2 / LIBC)
  [BOX64] Warning, function my_glob not found          (3x per pass)

Root cause: the x86_64 wine flavor is bionic-linked and runs its whole
x86_64-bionic dependency closure EMULATED (BOX64_PREFER_EMULATED=1, the
closure ships in the wine package at lib/x86_64-bionic/). The bionic libs
reference bionic-only symbols that box64's wrappedlibc map (glibc-host
oriented) does not carry and no host dlopen provides:
  * __FD_SET_chk / __FD_CLR_chk / __FD_ISSET_chk  - bionic select(2)
    fortify (libc.map.txt LIBC; declared in <sys/select.h>)
  * __gnu_strerror_r                              - GNU strerror_r
    (libc.map.txt LIBC, API 23+; <string.h> renames strerror_r to it)
  * __android_log_print / __android_log_write /
    __android_log_is_loggable / __android_log_buf_write - liblog, and
    box64 links only c/m/dl so the host dlsym has no provider
  * __fseterr                                    - bionic stdio_ext
    (libc.map.txt LIBC_P, API 28+; libunistring)
  * __strchr_chk / __strrchr_chk / __strlen_chk / __strlcat_chk /
    __strncpy_chk2 / __stpncpy_chk2               - bionic string
    fortify family (libc.map.txt LIBC; libx265 & friends)
  * __system_property_get / __system_property_find / __system_property_read /
    __system_property_set                          - bionic system
    properties (libc.map.txt LIBC; libglib-2.0 / libicuuc)
  * glob / glob64                                  - the wrappedlibc map
    carries GOM(glob)/GOM(glob64) unconditionally, but upstream
    wrappedlibc.c compiles my_glob/my_glob64 under "#ifndef ANDROID"
    (glibc glob64) - every ANDROID build warns and leaves the PLT
    unwrapped
(The __errno_location / libz.so.1 error is the App-side
BOX64_LD_LIBRARY_PATH ordering bug - fixed in WineEnvironment.kt v3.4.4;
glibc libs must never shadow the bionic closure. This patch covers what
remains after that fix.)

Each unresolved JUMP_SLOT keeps its GOT slot pointing at the lazy PLT
stub; the first real call lands back in the resolver, fails again and
aborts/returns garbage - exactly the "wineboot stuck / nothing opens
after the prefix build" device symptoms (Xlib select paths, fontconfig
strerror paths, shmem error logging).

Fix mechanism - identical to the proven 0001 shm bridge:
  1. src/libtools/android_bionic_compat.c (new, compiles empty unless
     ANDROID): my_* entry points with default visibility (the
     -fvisibility=hidden + --gc-sections lesson of v3.2.21: they MUST be
     default-visibility .dynsym exports or the runtime bridge
     dlsym(dlopen(NULL), "my_<name>") in library.c getSymbolInSymbolMaps
     cannot find them). Plain libc symbols are direct calls into the
     bionic libc box64 itself is linked against (it exports them);
     liblog is dlopen("liblog.so")-ed lazily once (public NDK lib,
     always loadable from an app process) and forwarded through
     __android_log_vprint for the varargs bridge. glob forwards to
     bionic glob() (API 28+; LP64 glob_t layout is identical
     x86_64-bionic <-> aarch64-bionic) and wraps only the errfunc
     callback through RunFunctionFmt trampolines (upstream
     findgloberrFct is static in wrappedlibc.c, hence self-contained
     copies here). bionic-only prototypes are declared locally (void*
     for the opaque prop_info/FILE) so NDK header availability guards
     cannot bite; all signatures verified against AOSP bionic
     libc/mapfile/libc.map.txt + libc/include.
  2. wrappedlibc_private.h: GOM() switch under #ifdef ANDROID - the
     wrapped-libc map answers these names for any emulated lib (the
     plain-name fallback in getSymbolInMaps also covers the versioned
     "@LIBC"/"@LIBC_P" lookups the bionic closure emits).
  3. CMakeLists.txt: compile the new file into ELFLOADER_SRC on ANDROID.

REBUILD_WRAPPERS.PY CONSTRAINT (v3.4.5, box64-build-log-aarch64(9).zip):
  rebuild_wrappers.py readFiles()/add_symbol_name() requires every
  function registered inside an #ifdef branch to also be registered
  under the matching #else branch, or the whole build aborts at the
  WRAPPERS step with "NotImplementedError: Some functions are only
  implemented under one condition (probably)
  (defined(ANDROID):wrappedlibc_private.h)" - before any C file
  compiles (make Error, functions_list.txt generation).
  The parser picks names out of commented "//GOM(name," lines too
  (its "GO in ln" fallback branch), which is exactly how upstream
  balances its own Android-only __libc_init/__errno block in this
  same header. The #else branch below therefore lists ALL nineteen
  names commented out - the pairing moves them to the unconditional
  symbol set while the GOM entries (and their generated wrapper map
  rows) stay guarded by defined(ANDROID) for bionic builds only.
  Verified locally: rebuild_wrappers.py with the CMakeLists argument
  set ("PANDORA HAVE_LD80BITS NOALIGN HAVE_TRACE ANDROID TERMUX
  STATICBUILD LA64 PPC64LE --" + wrapped headers) runs clean with the
  extended block, functions_list.txt gains all new names.

Wrapper signatures verified against v0.4.4 src/wrapped/generated/wrapper.h
(iFEpppV / vFipL / iFipL / pFipL / iFipp / iFipi / iFiipp all exist;
vFEpppV does NOT, so __android_log_assert is left out on purpose; the
new batch adds vFp / pFpiL / LFpL / LFppLL / pFppLL / iFpp / pFp /
iFppp - all present).
Hunks generated by GNU diff against a v0.4.4 tree carrying 0001..0007
(0001 with its documented default-fuzz placement; on v0.4.4 the twins
0003/0005/0006/0007 correctly skip) - applies with --fuzz=0 after them.
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -495,6 +495,7 @@
     # kernels often lack CONFIG_SYSVIPC) - see src/libtools/android_shmem.c
     list(APPEND ELFLOADER_SRC
         "${BOX64_ROOT}/src/libtools/android_shmem.c"
+        "${BOX64_ROOT}/src/libtools/android_bionic_compat.c"
         )
 endif()
 if(NOT STATICBUILD)
diff --git a/src/libtools/android_bionic_compat.c b/src/libtools/android_bionic_compat.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/libtools/android_bionic_compat.c
@@ -0,0 +1,291 @@
+/*****************************************************************************
+ * LinBox addition (0008): bionic-only symbol bridges for the x86_64-bionic
+ * dependency closure (ANDROID builds only).
+ *
+ * Why this file exists (user device log 2026-11-14, containers 000/1080):
+ *   The x86_64 wine flavor is bionic-linked; the x86_64-bionic dependency
+ *   closure shipped inside the wine package (lib/x86_64-bionic: libX11.so,
+ *   libfontconfig.so, libandroid-shmem.so, ...) runs EMULATED under box64
+ *   with BOX64_PREFER_EMULATED=1.  Their bionic-only PLT references have
+ *   no provider in a glibc-host-oriented wrappedlibc map:
+ *     * libX11.so           -> __FD_SET_chk / __FD_ISSET_chk (bionic
+ *                              select(2) fortify, libc.map LIBC)
+ *     * libfontconfig.so    -> __gnu_strerror_r (GNU strerror_r, API 23+)
+ *     * libandroid-shmem.so -> __android_log_print (liblog)
+ *   Every unresolved JUMP_SLOT leaves the GOT slot pointing at the lazy
+ *   PLT stub ("Error: Symbol ... not found, cannot apply
+ *   R_X86_64_JUMP_SLOT"); the first real call lands back in the resolver
+ *   and dies - the "wineboot stuck / nothing opens after the prefix
+ *   build" device symptoms (Xlib select paths, fontconfig strerror paths,
+ *   shmem error logging).
+ *
+ * What this file provides (same mechanism as android_shmem.c / 0001):
+ *   my_* entry points, default-visibility .dynsym exports, discovered at
+ *   runtime by the wrapped-libc bridge (library.c getSymbolInSymbolMaps:
+ *   dlsym(dlopen(NULL), "my_<name>"), registered through the GOM() switch
+ *   in wrappedlibc_private.h).  Plain libc symbols are direct calls into
+ *   the bionic libc box64 itself is linked against; liblog is dlopen()ed
+ *   lazily (box64 links only c/m/dl upstream).
+ *
+ * This file compiles EMPTY unless ANDROID is defined: glibc-form box64
+ * keeps upstream behavior untouched.
+ *****************************************************************************/
+
+#ifdef ANDROID
+
+#define _GNU_SOURCE
+#include <dlfcn.h>
+#include <glob.h>
+#include <pthread.h>
+#include <stdarg.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <sys/select.h>
+#include <sys/types.h>
+
+#include "x64emu.h"
+#include "box64cpu.h"
+#include "callback.h"             /* RunFunctionFmt (glob errfunc trampoline) */
+#include "emu/x64emu_private.h" /* full x64emu_s (scratch) + regs.h (R_EAX) */
+#include "myalign.h"
+
+/* Force default visibility: box64 builds with -fvisibility=hidden globally;
+ * hidden globals never reach .dynsym and are --gc-sections fodder - the
+ * wrapped-libc bridge would not find the my_* aliases (same lesson as
+ * android_shmem.c's ANW_EXPORT, v3.2.21). */
+#define LBC_EXPORT __attribute__((visibility("default")))
+
+/* ---- bionic libc prototypes ------------------------------------------- */
+/* __FD_SET_chk / __FD_CLR_chk / __FD_ISSET_chk are declared by bionic's
+ * <sys/select.h> (already included above).  __gnu_strerror_r is only
+ * referenced there via __RENAME(strerror_r), so declare it ourselves:
+ * exported by the DEVICE libc since API 23 (libc.map.txt, version LIBC).
+ *
+ * 0008 ext (2026-11-14 device logs, containers 92 / 10889): the next
+ * bionic-only batch, all exported by the device libc (libc.map.txt: base
+ * LIBC block, except __fseterr/glob which are LIBC_P since API 28 - box64
+ * targets api=28).  Declared locally with void* for the opaque prop_info /
+ * FILE pointers so <sys/system_properties.h>/<stdio_ext.h> availability
+ * guards cannot bite; the string *_chk prototypes are ABI-identical
+ * compatible redeclarations of bionic <string.h>'s. */
+__BEGIN_DECLS
+char* __gnu_strerror_r(int errnum, char* buf, size_t n);
+void   __fseterr(void* fp);                                   /* (FILE*) - bionic stdio_ext, API 28+ */
+char*  __strchr_chk(const char* s, int c, size_t s_len);
+char*  __strrchr_chk(const char* s, int c, size_t s_len);
+size_t __strlen_chk(const char* s, size_t s_len);
+size_t __strlcat_chk(char* dst, const char* src, size_t size, size_t dst_len);
+char*  __strncpy_chk2(char* dst, const char* src, size_t n, size_t dst_len, size_t src_len);
+char*  __stpncpy_chk2(char* dst, const char* src, size_t n, size_t dst_len, size_t src_len);
+int    __system_property_get(const char* name, char* value);
+void*  __system_property_find(const char* name);              /* const prop_info* (opaque) */
+int    __system_property_read(void* pi, char* name, char* value);
+int    __system_property_set(const char* name, const char* value);
+__END_DECLS
+
+/* ---- liblog (dlopen'd once: box64 links only c/m/dl) ------------------ */
+typedef int (*linbox_log_vprint_t)(int prio, const char* tag,
+                                   const char* fmt, va_list ap);
+typedef int (*linbox_log_write_t)(int prio, const char* tag, const char* text);
+typedef int (*linbox_log_islog_t)(int prio, const char* tag, int def);
+typedef int (*linbox_log_bufwrite_t)(int bufID, int prio, const char* tag,
+                                     const char* text);
+
+static pthread_once_t g_lbc_log_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+static linbox_log_vprint_t   g_lbc_vprint;
+static linbox_log_write_t    g_lbc_write;
+static linbox_log_islog_t    g_lbc_islog;
+static linbox_log_bufwrite_t g_lbc_bufwrite;
+
+static void linbox_log_init(void)
+{
+    void* h = dlopen("liblog.so", RTLD_LAZY | RTLD_GLOBAL);
+    if (!h) return;
+    g_lbc_vprint   = (linbox_log_vprint_t)dlsym(h, "__android_log_vprint");
+    g_lbc_write    = (linbox_log_write_t)dlsym(h, "__android_log_write");
+    g_lbc_islog    = (linbox_log_islog_t)dlsym(h, "__android_log_is_loggable");
+    g_lbc_bufwrite = (linbox_log_bufwrite_t)dlsym(h, "__android_log_buf_write");
+}
+
+/* ---- bridges (my_* names are dlsym'ed by the GOM map) ------------------ */
+
+LBC_EXPORT void my___FD_SET_chk(int fd, fd_set* set, size_t set_size)
+{
+    __FD_SET_chk(fd, set, set_size);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT void my___FD_CLR_chk(int fd, fd_set* set, size_t set_size)
+{
+    __FD_CLR_chk(fd, set, set_size);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT int my___FD_ISSET_chk(int fd, fd_set* set, size_t set_size)
+{
+    return __FD_ISSET_chk(fd, set, set_size);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT char* my___gnu_strerror_r(int errnum, char* buf, size_t n)
+{
+    return __gnu_strerror_r(errnum, buf, n);
+}
+
+/* varargs: the emulated x86_64 varargs area is rebuilt into emu->scratch
+ * (myStackAlign + PREPARE_VALIST), then handed to __android_log_vprint.
+ * NOTE: prio rides in a 'p' slot of the iFEpppV wrapper - a 32-bit
+ * sub-register write on x86_64 zero-extends, so the full 64-bit read is
+ * the correct value (upstream __asprintf/iFEppV uses the same trick). */
+LBC_EXPORT int my___android_log_print(x64emu_t* emu, void* vprio,
+                                      void* tag, void* fmt, void* b)
+{
+    pthread_once(&g_lbc_log_once, linbox_log_init);
+    if (!g_lbc_vprint) return 0;
+    myStackAlign(emu, (const char*)fmt, b, emu->scratch, R_EAX, 3);
+    PREPARE_VALIST;
+    return g_lbc_vprint((int)(uintptr_t)vprio, (const char*)tag,
+                        (const char*)fmt, VARARGS);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT int my___android_log_write(int prio, void* tag, void* text)
+{
+    pthread_once(&g_lbc_log_once, linbox_log_init);
+    if (!g_lbc_write) return 0;
+    return g_lbc_write(prio, (const char*)tag, (const char*)text);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT int my___android_log_is_loggable(int prio, void* tag, int def)
+{
+    pthread_once(&g_lbc_log_once, linbox_log_init);
+    if (!g_lbc_islog) return (prio >= def) ? 1 : 0;
+    return g_lbc_islog(prio, (const char*)tag, def);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT int my___android_log_buf_write(int bufID, int prio,
+                                          void* tag, void* text)
+{
+    pthread_once(&g_lbc_log_once, linbox_log_init);
+    if (!g_lbc_bufwrite) return 0;
+    return g_lbc_bufwrite(bufID, prio, (const char*)tag, (const char*)text);
+}
+
+/* ---- bionic-only libc bridges (0008 ext, 2026-11-14 device logs) --------
+ * Direct forwards into the bionic libc box64 itself is linked against
+ * (identical pattern to my___gnu_strerror_r above; the device libc exports
+ * every one of them - see the prototype block for libc.map.txt provenance):
+ *   libunistring.so -> __fseterr                       (containers 92/10889)
+ *   libglib-2.0.so  -> __system_property_get           (containers 92/10889)
+ *   libicuuc.so.78  -> __system_property_find          (container 10889)
+ *   libx265.so      -> __strchr_chk / __strlen_chk     (container 10889)
+ * plus the same-family fortify / property entries bridged proactively so
+ * the next closure lib that references them resolves instead of aborting
+ * on its first call through an unresolved lazy PLT stub. */
+
+LBC_EXPORT void my___fseterr(void* fp)
+{
+    __fseterr(fp);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT char* my___strchr_chk(void* s, int c, size_t s_len)
+{
+    return __strchr_chk((const char*)s, c, s_len);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT char* my___strrchr_chk(void* s, int c, size_t s_len)
+{
+    return __strrchr_chk((const char*)s, c, s_len);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT size_t my___strlen_chk(void* s, size_t s_len)
+{
+    return __strlen_chk((const char*)s, s_len);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT size_t my___strlcat_chk(void* dst, void* src, size_t size,
+                                   size_t dst_len)
+{
+    return __strlcat_chk((char*)dst, (const char*)src, size, dst_len);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT char* my___strncpy_chk2(void* dst, void* src, size_t n,
+                                   size_t dst_len, size_t src_len)
+{
+    return __strncpy_chk2((char*)dst, (const char*)src, n, dst_len, src_len);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT char* my___stpncpy_chk2(void* dst, void* src, size_t n,
+                                   size_t dst_len, size_t src_len)
+{
+    return __stpncpy_chk2((char*)dst, (const char*)src, n, dst_len, src_len);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT int my___system_property_get(void* name, void* value)
+{
+    return __system_property_get((const char*)name, (char*)value);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT void* my___system_property_find(void* name)
+{
+    return __system_property_find((const char*)name);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT int my___system_property_read(void* pi, void* name, void* value)
+{
+    return __system_property_read(pi, (char*)name, (char*)value);
+}
+
+LBC_EXPORT int my___system_property_set(void* name, void* value)
+{
+    return __system_property_set((const char*)name, (const char*)value);
+}
+
+/* ---- glob / glob64 ------------------------------------------------------
+ * Upstream wrappedlibc.c compiles my_glob/my_glob64 under "#ifndef ANDROID"
+ * (glibc glob64); the GOM(glob)/GOM(glob64) map entries in
+ * wrappedlibc_private.h are unconditional, so ANDROID builds emit
+ * "Warning, function my_glob not found" for every emulated lib that
+ * references glob() (container 10889 log: 3x per wineboot pass).
+ * bionic ships glob() since API 28 (libc.map.txt LIBC_P; no glob64 - the
+ * two map rows share the forwarder) and the LP64 glob_t layout is
+ * identical on x86_64-bionic and aarch64-bionic, so forward directly and
+ * wrap only the errfunc callback: it is an x86_64 code pointer that must
+ * re-enter the emulator (RunFunctionFmt), same trampoline scheme as
+ * upstream findgloberrFct - self-contained here because that helper is
+ * static in wrappedlibc.c. */
+#define LBC_GLOBERR_SLOTS 4
+static uintptr_t g_lbc_globerr_fct[LBC_GLOBERR_SLOTS];
+static int g_lbc_globerr_next;
+static int lbc_globerr_0(const char* epath, int eerrno) { return (int)RunFunctionFmt(g_lbc_globerr_fct[0], "pi", epath, eerrno); }
+static int lbc_globerr_1(const char* epath, int eerrno) { return (int)RunFunctionFmt(g_lbc_globerr_fct[1], "pi", epath, eerrno); }
+static int lbc_globerr_2(const char* epath, int eerrno) { return (int)RunFunctionFmt(g_lbc_globerr_fct[2], "pi", epath, eerrno); }
+static int lbc_globerr_3(const char* epath, int eerrno) { return (int)RunFunctionFmt(g_lbc_globerr_fct[3], "pi", epath, eerrno); }
+static int (*const lbc_globerr_fns[LBC_GLOBERR_SLOTS])(const char*, int) = {
+    lbc_globerr_0, lbc_globerr_1, lbc_globerr_2, lbc_globerr_3,
+};
+static int (*lbc_findgloberrFct(void* fct))(const char*, int)
+{
+    int i;
+    if (!fct) return NULL;
+    for (i = 0; i < LBC_GLOBERR_SLOTS; ++i)
+        if (g_lbc_globerr_fct[i] == (uintptr_t)fct)
+            return lbc_globerr_fns[i];
+    i = g_lbc_globerr_next;
+    g_lbc_globerr_next = (g_lbc_globerr_next + 1) % LBC_GLOBERR_SLOTS;
+    g_lbc_globerr_fct[i] = (uintptr_t)fct;
+    return lbc_globerr_fns[i];
+}
+LBC_EXPORT int32_t my_glob64(x64emu_t* emu, void* pat, int32_t flags,
+                             void* errfnc, void* pglob)
+{
+    (void)emu;
+    return glob((const char*)pat, flags, lbc_findgloberrFct(errfnc),
+                (glob_t*)pglob);
+}
+LBC_EXPORT int32_t my_glob(x64emu_t* emu, void* pat, int32_t flags,
+                           void* errfnc, void* pglob)
+{
+    (void)emu;
+    return glob((const char*)pat, flags, lbc_findgloberrFct(errfnc),
+                (glob_t*)pglob);
+}
+
+#endif /* ANDROID */
diff --git a/src/wrapped/wrappedlibc_private.h b/src/wrapped/wrappedlibc_private.h
--- a/src/wrapped/wrappedlibc_private.h
+++ b/src/wrapped/wrappedlibc_private.h
@@ -1873,6 +1873,69 @@
 GO(shmdt, iFp)
 GO(shmget, iFiLi)
 #endif
+#ifdef ANDROID
+// LinBox (0008): bionic-only symbols referenced by the x86_64-bionic
+// dependency closure (libX11.so __FD_*_chk, libfontconfig.so
+// __gnu_strerror_r, libandroid-shmem.so / liblog __android_log_*) but
+// absent from the glibc-host map - bridge to the native compat in
+// src/libtools/android_bionic_compat.c (my_* via dlsym, see library.c
+// getSymbolInSymbolMaps; the plain-name fallback also covers the
+// versioned "@LIBC"/"@LIBC_P" lookups the bionic closure emits).
+GOM(__FD_CLR_chk, vFipL)
+GOM(__FD_SET_chk, vFipL)
+GOM(__FD_ISSET_chk, iFipL)
+GOM(__gnu_strerror_r, pFipL)
+GOM(__android_log_print, iFEpppV)
+GOM(__android_log_write, iFipp)
